  "details": "Ever since SDK3 avatars have released, I have experienced issues where if I jump while standing still in full body and in an SDK3 avatar, tracking control is given to animation instead of full body trackers which leads to the jump animation taking control over the chest and lower body even if no tracking control components are taking control over the chest or lower body. This seems to be an issue on on other tracking points as well. I have modified the default base layer to disable sub state transitions to test this on desktop and 3 point tracking and a \"snapping\" effect occurs on all of them when the animator \"should\" be transitioning between landing and restoring tracking control. This is most easily tested in full body and occurs on all avatars if you initially load into a world with an SDK3 avatar or switch into an SDK3 avatar from SDK2. Loading into a world with an SDK2 avatar does not cause this issue. Switching from an SDK3 avatar to SDK2 also causes this issue",
